# Baloth Prime enters tapped with six stun counters (CR 122.1d). On turn 2 Bot2 cracks its own fetchland: that is an
# opponent sacrificing a land, so nothing triggers. Bot1's untap step on turn 3 takes a stun counter off instead of
# untapping it (6 -> 5). Bot1 then sacrifices Misty Rainforest to its own ability, which triggers Baloth Prime: a tapped
# 4/4 Beast, and "untap this creature" takes off another counter (4). Baloth's own "{4}, Sacrifice a land" gains 2 life
# and triggers it again (3), with a second tapped Beast. Life: 20 - 1 (fetch) + 2 = 21.

